@meta
id: 18-15
title: Scenario — the email that never sent
chapter: 18
type: scenario
skills: edit-file, find-path, wildmenu, buffer-switch, search-slash
par: 235
minutes: 12
vscode: three tabs and the sidebar
vimrc: set path=.,** wildmenu wildmode=longest:full,full
open: src/domain/order/order.provider.ts

@brief
A ticket, not an exercise.

    ORD-507  Customers are not told when an order is cancelled.
             EmailService is injected into OrderProvider and registered
             in the container, and nothing ever calls it. Send the
             cancellation email after the refund. While you are there,
             the code the email service throws is not in the error
             table: it should throw EMAIL_SEND_FAILED, and that code
             needs registering as a 502 that alerts.

One file is open. You find the rest. `path` and `wildmenu` are set.

  1. order.provider.ts — in `cancel`, directly after the refund line:

         await this.emailService.sendOrderCancelled({ orderId: order.id });

  2. The email service — it currently throws `EMAIL_FAILED`. Make it
     `EMAIL_SEND_FAILED`. Its import is right there in the provider.

  3. default.json — add, as the last entry:

         "EMAIL_SEND_FAILED": { "statusCode": 502, "sentry": true }

     Mind the comma on the line above it.

The registry and the payment service are correct. Leave them alone.

@keys
| `gf` | open the file whose path is under the cursor |
| `:find name` `Tab` | find a file by name, anywhere in `path` |
| `:w` | write before you leave a buffer |
| `Ctrl-O` | back to where you jumped from |

@hints
Do the provider first while you are in it. `/refund(` puts you on the
refund call; `o` opens the line below with the right indent. Write it.
--
The email service import is four lines from the top of the provider.
Put the cursor on its path and `gf`. Search for `EMAIL_`, then `fF`
and insert `SEND_` before it.
--
You know the error table is `default.json` and you do not care where it
is: `:find def` Tab. `/REFUND` gets you to the last entry; `$a,` adds
the comma; `o` and the new entry.
--
Par assumes each line is typed once. Nothing here needs a visual
selection or a register.

@solution
A reasonable route, file by file.

**order.provider.ts** — `/refund(` Enter, `o`, the `sendOrderCancelled`
line, `Esc`, `:w`.

**email.service.ts** — `/email.service` Enter puts you on the import,
`gf` opens it. `/EMAIL_` Enter, `fF`, `iSEND_`, `Esc`, `:w`.

**default.json** — `:find def` Tab Enter. `/REFUND` Enter, `$a,` `Esc`,
`o`, the new entry, `Esc`, `:wq`.

Three files, three different ways of reaching them, and none of them
was a path typed in full. The provider was open. The service was one
`gf` away because the provider imports it. The error table was a name
you knew and a directory you did not, which is exactly what `:find` is
for.

That is the pattern for the whole chapter: the file you want is almost
always either imported by the one you are in, or has a name you can
half-remember. Reach for `gf` first, `:find` second, and the browser
only when you genuinely do not know what you are looking for.

@start src/domain/order/order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../../infrastructure/services/email.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(EmailService) protected emailService: EmailService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected src/domain/order/order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../../infrastructure/services/email.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(EmailService) protected emailService: EmailService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);
    await this.emailService.sendOrderCancelled({ orderId: order.id });

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@start src/infrastructure/services/email.service.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';

@injectable()
export class EmailService {
  public async sendOrderCancelled(args: { orderId: string }) {
    const response = await this.http.post(`/email/order-cancelled`, args);

    if (response.status !== 202) {
      throw exception('EMAIL_FAILED');
    }

    return response.data;
  }
}

@expected src/infrastructure/services/email.service.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';

@injectable()
export class EmailService {
  public async sendOrderCancelled(args: { orderId: string }) {
    const response = await this.http.post(`/email/order-cancelled`, args);

    if (response.status !== 202) {
      throw exception('EMAIL_SEND_FAILED');
    }

    return response.data;
  }
}

